Subject: [PATCH] A design reference for Classic that cannot rot
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds design/ : a contact sheet, a component and token system page, and four
proposed screens (Play, a reserve selected, a result, settings).

The pages load ../styles.css and ../ui.css before their own design.css, so every
swatch is var(--token) and every component is the shipped class. A reference that
restates the tokens is a second source of truth, and the copy is what rots.

Nothing in the app links here, nothing in src/ imports from here, and design/ is
not in the service worker's SHELL — so no CACHE bump is needed. DECISIONS.md
records that boundary; the moment it stops holding, this stops being a reference.

Two additions are marked PROPOSED in design.css and do not ship: .square.refused,
and the brand mark as an image rather than the Arial letterform tile.

Measured first, so the screens answer something. The first action is below the
fold on every viewport (7px at 390x844, 205px at 360x640, 125px at 1440x900);
.lobby-play is display:none below 761px so a phone has no route to a game; and a
drop that would give check is refused in silence — with a rook in hand against a
black king on b4, the six refused squares are exactly rank 4 and the b-file.

DEVLOG has the full entry, including what was rejected: implementing the IA in
this pass, and shipping a design/tokens.css for the app to import.

